    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a constrained roster, as key offensive pillars like **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** are sidelined by team off-days. Consequently, **Kyle Tucker** emerges as our premier start with a score of 67.65. While Gasser presents a moderate challenge, **Kyle Tucker** maintains an elite baseline profile, bolstered by a 4% premium for his role in the four-hole and a slight boost derived from Gasser\u2019s 4.14 xERA. His consistency remains our best hedge against a limited daily ceiling.\n\nRounding out the active group, **Andy Pages** earns a start with a 59.38 score, hovering just below our \"Strong\" tier threshold. The decision to roster **Andy Pages** over potential fringe alternatives was heavily influenced by Gasser\u2019s slow delivery tempo, which historically increases the opportunity for stolen bases\u2014a critical factor given our strategic emphasis on SB scarcity. While **Luis Robert Jr.** remains anchored to the IL, the rest of our bench depth, including **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Franklin Arias**, offers no viable production today due to scheduling gaps. We remain heavily reliant on **Kyle Tucker** to drive our core categories while looking for **Andy Pages** to capitalize on his favorable matchup conditions.",
